course: dictionary
lesson: 4445
title: Handwriting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Handwriting is writing that you make by hand, with a pen or pencil, not typed on a keyboard. It can also mean the way a person's writing looks, such as neat or messy. «Use your best handwriting» means: write so that every letter can be read easily.
explain: Handwriting is uncountable, so we do not say "a handwriting" the way we say "a pencil". We talk about «neat handwriting» or «messy handwriting». The words around it give the clue: when a sentence says a recipe was in Grandma's handwriting, it means the way Grandma's writing looks.
explain: In school, handwriting lessons teach letter shapes, joined-up writing and neat spacing. In stories, detectives can recognise who wrote a note by its handwriting, because each person's writing is a little bit different.
fact: Handwriting means writing done by hand with a pen or pencil.
fact: Handwriting can also mean the way a person's writing looks, such as «neat handwriting».
fact: «Joined-up handwriting» means writing where the letters are joined together.
fact: Handwriting is marked separately from composition: presentation is how neat your writing looks, and composition is what you write and how well you write it.
fact: Detectives sometimes recognise who wrote a note by its handwriting.
exercise: «Then she found an old recipe in Grandma's handwriting.» What does handwriting mean here? | Old paper with no words | *The way Grandma's writing looks | A recipe book printed in a shop | Cooking with Mum on Sunday
exercise: «Use your best handwriting» means the teacher wants you to... | *Write neatly, so every letter can be read | Type your work on the computer | Write as fast as you can, even if it is messy | Draw pictures instead of writing
exercise: In «clues like chocolate on faces, handwriting or screen-time records», which word is about writing by hand? | records | faces | chocolate | *handwriting
test: The paper was «not in the Knave's handwriting and not signed.» What does this tell us? | The paper was written by the Knave | The paper was printed by a machine | The paper was signed by the Knave | *The writing did not look like the Knave's writing
test: Fill the gap: Her ___ was neat, so everyone could read her notes. | *handwriting | keyboard | typing | spelling
exam: Which sentence uses handwriting to mean the way writing looks? | The keyboard is broken again | *Her neat handwriting made the note easy to read | The shop sells typed letters | He drew a picture of a dog
